# ONNX Runtime's native bridge resolves these Java classes, constructors and fields by their
# original names. The 1.27.0 Android AAR carries no consumer keep rules, so full-mode R8 otherwise
# renames the Java side successfully and inference aborts in JNI at GetMethodID/FindClass time.
# The whole bridge is only ~120 KiB of bytecode and this package-level boundary also covers output
# types added by future ONNX Runtime updates.
-keep class ai.onnxruntime.** { *; }

# review-ktx 2.0.2's `OnSuccessListener` SAM wrapper carries a runtime parameter annotation copied
# from an internal Play services build. No published play-services-basement defines the class, and
# R8 fails the release on the missing reference. ART skips annotations it cannot resolve, so the
# missing class costs nothing at runtime.
-dontwarn com.google.android.gms.common.annotation.NoNullnessRewrite
